task-116 benchmark Run gate + seed requirement

ROOT CAUSE
features/models/routes.ts disabled Run with !selected.has(judge); update.ts BenchmarkRunRequested
repeated the same check. The :3456 reference (control-benchmark.tsx:527-532) only requires
selectedCount >= 2, a non-empty runnable judge, and !running; the judge need not be a graded subject.

FIX
- routes.ts: removed !selected.has(judge); restored the overlap warning in the reference wording
  when the judge is one of the selected subjects.
- update.ts: BenchmarkRunRequested now rejects only <2 selected or an empty judge; accepts an
external judge and posts it as judgeEndpointId.

RED (s622-benchmark-red.log): 2 failed / 10 passed - external-judge Run was blocked and the
overlap warning rendered for a non-overlapping judge because the fixture selected every endpoint.
GREEN (s622-benchmark-green.log): 12/12. Covers external judge enabled + exact body, overlap warning,
empty judge disabled, <2 subjects disabled, running disabled.

SEED GAP
benchmark endpointOptions/runnableEntries are fed ONLY by READBACK_SPECS.modelEndpoints
(GET /api/role-model/endpoints). Models existing in /api/role-model/models or routing candidates do
NOT populate the page. On the seeded instance that readback is empty, so the page honestly renders
"No runnable endpoints" and "0 of 0 selected".

Build-lane seed requirement (no seeder change here): seed /api/role-model/endpoints with >= 2 entries
of shape { endpointId, modelId, sourceType, healthStatus, benchmarkEligible: true } (or
benchmarkEligible absent + executionModeEligible != false); optional third endpoint as the dedicated
judge. Also seed /api/role-model/benchmark/suite with at least one benchmark_eligible:true,
quick_benchmark:true case so Quick counts are non-zero.
